IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `acnc-registration`

-- Australian Charities and Not-for-profits Commission Act 2012, Part 2-1, ss 40-5, 40-10, 160-10 -- worked cases.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked
-- against a decided case or subsidiary legislation (none was retrieved).
--
-- Fixtures are generated from a table of which flags are set (scratchpad gen_australian-charities-and-not-for-profits-commission-act-2012_baseline.py). Expected results were written by
-- hand from the text.

-- Facts from the WA life of Daniel (workbench scenarios au/wa/cradle-to-grave-daniel): on 1 March 2051 Daniel founds the Rossi
-- Foundation, a private ancillary fund registered with the ACNC, with deductible gift recipient status, and gives it $2,000,000
-- (d072); on 3 May 2076 the Foundation's trustee company passes to his children, Anjali and Luca (d091).
-- Consistent with the Taxation Administration Act 1953 baseline (s 426-105(1)(a)): a private ancillary fund is a trust whose every
-- trustee is a constitutional corporation -- here one trustee company, of which Daniel is a director.
-- HYPOTHETICAL (the scenario does not say): the application is made 1 March 2051 and registration takes effect that day; the
-- subtype is advancing social or public welfare; the $2,000,000 gift is the Foundation's revenue for 2050-51 (INFERENCE: a donation
-- is revenue under the accounting standards -- a borrowed measure, asked as a fact); revenue in 2075-76 is $120,000; Daniel resigns
-- as a director on 3 May 2076 and Anjali and Luca are appointed; a penalty unit of $330 (Crimes Act 1914 s 4AA, before indexation).
-- The text encoded is the 2025 compilation, not the law as it will stand in 2051 or 2076.

`d072: the Rossi Foundation` MEANS `My foundation` WITH
    `it is a not-for-profit entity` IS TRUE
    `it is a charity under the Charities Act 2013` IS TRUE
    `it complies with the governance standards` IS TRUE
    `it complies with the external conduct standards` IS TRUE
    `it has an ABN` IS TRUE
    `it is listed by a written decision as engaging in or supporting terrorist or criminal activity` IS FALSE
    `its registration was revoked before` IS FALSE
    `the Commissioner is satisfied the matters behind the revocation are dealt with` IS FALSE

`d072 variant: the Foundation not meeting a governance standard` MEANS `My foundation` WITH
    `it is a not-for-profit entity` IS TRUE
    `it is a charity under the Charities Act 2013` IS TRUE
    `it complies with the governance standards` IS FALSE
    `it complies with the external conduct standards` IS TRUE
    `it has an ABN` IS TRUE
    `it is listed by a written decision as engaging in or supporting terrorist or criminal activity` IS FALSE
    `its registration was revoked before` IS FALSE
    `the Commissioner is satisfied the matters behind the revocation are dealt with` IS FALSE

`a charity revoked before, the Commissioner not satisfied` MEANS `My foundation` WITH
    `it is a not-for-profit entity` IS TRUE
    `it is a charity under the Charities Act 2013` IS TRUE
    `it complies with the governance standards` IS TRUE
    `it complies with the external conduct standards` IS TRUE
    `it has an ABN` IS TRUE
    `it is listed by a written decision as engaging in or supporting terrorist or criminal activity` IS FALSE
    `its registration was revoked before` IS TRUE
    `the Commissioner is satisfied the matters behind the revocation are dealt with` IS FALSE

`a not-for-profit social club that is not a charity` MEANS `My foundation` WITH
    `it is a not-for-profit entity` IS TRUE
    `it is a charity under the Charities Act 2013` IS FALSE
    `it complies with the governance standards` IS TRUE
    `it complies with the external conduct standards` IS TRUE
    `it has an ABN` IS TRUE
    `it is listed by a written decision as engaging in or supporting terrorist or criminal activity` IS FALSE
    `its registration was revoked before` IS FALSE
    `the Commissioner is satisfied the matters behind the revocation are dealt with` IS FALSE

`the Commissioner believes the Foundation breaches a governance standard` MEANS `What the Commissioner reasonably believes` WITH
    `my foundation is or was not entitled to registration` IS FALSE
    `my foundation gave false or misleading information in its application` IS FALSE
    `my foundation contravened, or will likely contravene, the Act` IS FALSE
    `my foundation did not, or will likely not, comply with a governance or external conduct standard` IS TRUE
    `my foundation has a trustee in bankruptcy, liquidator or insolvency manager` IS FALSE
    `my foundation asked in the approved form for revocation` IS FALSE

`the Commissioner believes nothing against the Foundation` MEANS `What the Commissioner reasonably believes` WITH
    `my foundation is or was not entitled to registration` IS FALSE
    `my foundation gave false or misleading information in its application` IS FALSE
    `my foundation contravened, or will likely contravene, the Act` IS FALSE
    `my foundation did not, or will likely not, comply with a governance or external conduct standard` IS FALSE
    `my foundation has a trustee in bankruptcy, liquidator or insolvency manager` IS FALSE
    `my foundation asked in the approved form for revocation` IS FALSE

§ `s 25-5`

-- d072: the Rossi Foundation, a not-for-profit charity meeting the standards with an ABN, is entitled to registration as a
-- charity. Out of line with a governance standard, it is not. A charity revoked before needs the
-- Commissioner satisfied. A social club that is not a charity cannot register: the table has one type, "Charity".
#ASSERT `Is my foundation entitled to registration as a charity` `d072: the Rossi Foundation`
#ASSERT NOT `Is my foundation entitled to registration as a charity` `d072 variant: the Foundation not meeting a governance standard`
#ASSERT NOT `Is my foundation entitled to registration as a charity` `a charity revoked before, the Commissioner not satisfied`
#ASSERT NOT `Is my foundation entitled to registration as a charity` `a not-for-profit social club that is not a charity`

-- d072: the subtype (advancing social or public welfare, HYPOTHETICAL) needs registration as a charity first: not yet registered, not yet entitled.
#ASSERT NOT `Is my foundation entitled to registration as the subtype` `d072: the Rossi Foundation` `advancing social or public welfare` TRUE FALSE

§ `s 30-20`

-- d072: an application in the approved form, with the information the Commissioner asked for, must be granted. Not if the
-- information was not given.
#ASSERT `Must the Commissioner register my foundation` `d072: the Rossi Foundation` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Must the Commissioner register my foundation` `d072: the Rossi Foundation` TRUE TRUE FALSE

§ `s 30-15(3)`

-- d072: applied 1 March 2051. With no request for information, the time ends at the end of 30 April 2051 (the 60th day).
-- Information asked for and last given 20 April 2051: 28 days later, 18 May 2051, is later, so it governs.
#ASSERT `When does the Commissioner's time to decide end` (Date 1 3 2051) FALSE (Date 1 3 2051) EQUALS (Date 30 4 2051)
#ASSERT `When does the Commissioner's time to decide end` (Date 1 3 2051) TRUE (Date 20 4 2051) EQUALS (Date 18 5 2051)

§ `ss 20-5, 30-30`

-- d072: registered with effect from 1 March 2051 (HYPOTHETICAL), the Foundation meets the registration prerequisite on 15
-- March 2051 but not on 28 February 2051.
#ASSERT `Is my foundation registered on the day` (Date 15 3 2051) TRUE (Date 1 3 2051) FALSE (Date 1 1 2100)
#ASSERT NOT `Is my foundation registered on the day` (Date 28 2 2051) TRUE (Date 1 3 2051) FALSE (Date 1 1 2100)

§ `s 35-10`

-- A reasonable belief in a breach of a governance standard is enough to allow revocation; no belief, no power.
#ASSERT `May the Commissioner revoke my foundation's registration` `the Commissioner believes the Foundation breaches a governance standard`

-- HYPOTHETICAL dates: entitlement lost 1 January 2060; registration effective 1 March 2051; revocation made 1 August 2060.
-- Notice of revocation is due within 14 days: 15 August 2060. (A false-information revocation may reach back to 1 March 2051.)
#ASSERT `From when can the revocation take effect at the earliest` `it is not entitled to registration` (Date 1 1 2060) (Date 1 3 2051) (Date 1 8 2060) EQUALS (Date 1 1 2060)
#ASSERT `From when can the revocation take effect at the earliest` `it gave false or misleading information in its application` (Date 1 1 2060) (Date 1 3 2051) (Date 1 8 2060) EQUALS (Date 1 3 2051)

#ASSERT `By when must my foundation be told of the revocation` (Date 1 8 2060) EQUALS (Date 15 8 2060)

§ `s 35-15`

-- d091: a show cause notice given 1 June 2076 (HYPOTHETICAL) leaves until 29 June 2076. None is owed if the Commissioner
-- believes on reasonable grounds that acting without one is appropriate.
#ASSERT NOT `Must my foundation be given a show cause notice` TRUE

#ASSERT `By when may my foundation show cause` (Date 1 6 2076) EQUALS (Date 29 6 2076)

§ `ss 40-5, 40-10`

-- d072: Daniel's name and position as a director of the trustee go on the public Register. d091: so do Anjali's and
-- Luca's. Not if the Commissioner has decided to leave it off under s 40-10(2).
#ASSERT `Will my name be on the Register` TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Will my name be on the Register` TRUE FALSE TRUE

§ `s 160-10`

-- d091: Daniel, removed as a responsible entity by a notice served 1 June 2076 (HYPOTHETICAL), objects by 31 July 2076. Lodged
-- 1 August with a request the Commissioner agrees to, it is treated as in time.
#ASSERT `By when must I object` (Date 1 6 2076) EQUALS (Date 31 7 2076)

#ASSERT `Is the objection in time` (Date 1 6 2076) (Date 31 7 2076) FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `Is the objection in time` (Date 1 6 2076) (Date 1 8 2076) TRUE TRUE

